{
  "version": 1,
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "c_t20001",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Outputs: look at a result and ask it questions",
        "",
        "Read a result as a tree, a grid or raw JSON, then query it with a filter, JSONPath, jq or SQL.",
        "",
        "You will also see where `console` output goes, how an error points at your line, how to draw a table or an image, and how to compare two runs of a cell. About 10 minutes.",
        "",
        "Click **Run All** in the toolbar (or press **Cmd+Shift+Enter**; Ctrl+Shift+Enter on Linux), then follow the steps. The last code cell fails on purpose."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20002",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. One result, three views",
        "",
        "The next cell builds the orders of a small, made-up tea shop. An array of objects like this one opens as a **grid**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20003",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "const orders = [",
        "  { id: 1, city: \"Lyon\", tea: \"green\", cups: 2, price: 3.5, status: \"paid\" },",
        "  { id: 2, city: \"Porto\", tea: \"black\", cups: 1, price: 3, status: \"paid\" },",
        "  { id: 3, city: \"Lyon\", tea: \"mint\", cups: 4, price: 4, status: \"refunded\" },",
        "  { id: 4, city: \"Ghent\", tea: \"green\", cups: 3, price: 3.5, status: \"paid\" },",
        "  { id: 5, city: \"Porto\", tea: \"oolong\", cups: 2, price: 5, status: \"pending\" },",
        "  { id: 6, city: \"Ghent\", tea: \"black\", cups: 6, price: 3, status: \"paid\" },",
        "  { id: 7, city: \"Lyon\", tea: \"oolong\", cups: 1, price: 5, status: \"paid\" },",
        "  { id: 8, city: \"Porto\", tea: \"mint\", cups: 2, price: 4, status: \"paid\" },",
        "];",
        "orders"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20004",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Above the grid, on the right, three buttons switch the view:",
        "",
        "- **Tree** shows the value as nested, foldable rows: good for objects with depth.",
        "- **Grid** shows an array of objects as a table. Click a column's name to sort by it.",
        "- **Raw** shows the JSON text.",
        "",
        "Hover the result to see its other buttons: **Find**, **Query**, **Copy**, **Export** (JSON, CSV and more), and **Full screen**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20005",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Ask the result a question",
        "",
        "Hover the grid and click **Query** (the funnel). A bar opens with four modes. Pick one, type the query and press **Enter**:",
        "",
        "- **Filter**: type a key (`cups`), pick a test (`>`) and type a value (`2`). The filter becomes a chip, and the grid keeps the three orders with more than two cups.",
        "- **JSONPath**: `$[?(@.status == \"paid\")]` keeps the paid orders. **Only matches** and **All** switch between the matching rows and every row.",
        "- **jq**: `map(select(.tea == \"green\")) | map(.cups) | add` adds up the cups of green tea: `5`.",
        "- **SQL**: the value is the table `t`. Try `SELECT city, sum(cups * price) AS revenue FROM t GROUP BY city ORDER BY revenue DESC`.",
        "",
        "When a query answers with a new value, a link beside it (**Back to rows**) shows the whole value again.",
        "",
        "In an empty query field, `?` shows example queries for the mode you picked.",
        "",
        "SQL runs on DuckDB inside the page. The first SQL query loads it, and DuckDB fetches its JSON reader from duckdb.org once, so that first query needs a network connection; the browser keeps both afterwards."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20006",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Printed output",
        "",
        "`console.log` writes to the cell's **Output**, as it would in a terminal; `console.warn` and `console.error` write to its **Error output**, in red. A cell can print and return a result: the printed lines come first. Lines show as they are printed, even while the cell still runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20007",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "console.log(\"checking\", orders.length, \"orders\");",
        "for (const city of [\"Lyon\", \"Porto\", \"Ghent\"]) {",
        "  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 400));",
        "  console.log(city, orders.filter((order) => order.city === city).length);",
        "}",
        "console.warn(\"2 orders are not paid\");",
        "\"done\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20008",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Tables and images",
        "",
        "`display` adds outputs of its own to a cell, beside its result. `display.table(rows, { columns })` draws rows as a grid with the columns you pick, in that order. `display.image(...)` takes an image's bytes, a URL, a file path or SVG markup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20009",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "display.table(orders, { columns: [\"city\", \"tea\", \"cups\"] });",
        "",
        "const cupsByCity = Object.entries(Object.groupBy(orders, (order) => order.city)).map(",
        "  ([city, rows]) => ({ city, cups: rows!.reduce((sum, order) => sum + order.cups, 0) }),",
        ");",
        "const bars = cupsByCity",
        "  .map(",
        "    ({ city, cups }, i) =>",
        "      `<rect x=\"70\" y=\"${i * 30 + 10}\" width=\"${cups * 25}\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#5b8def\"/>` +",
        "      `<text x=\"0\" y=\"${i * 30 + 25}\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\">${city}</text>`,",
        "  )",
        "  .join(\"\");",
        "display.image(`<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"360\" height=\"100\">${bars}</svg>`);",
        "cupsByCity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20010",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 5. Compare two runs",
        "",
        "Run the next cell with **Cmd+Enter**, then change `2` to `3` and run it again. Open the cell's menu (the **…** at the right of its header, or right-click the header) and choose **Compare with Previous Run**: the dialog shows what changed in the result between the two runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20011",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "const discount = 2;",
        "orders.map((order) => ({ id: order.id, total: order.cups * order.price - discount }))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20012",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 6. Errors point at your line",
        "",
        "The next cell defines a function. The cell after it calls the function with a tea the shop does not sell, so the call throws. That cell fails **on purpose**, and it is the last code cell for a reason: **Run All** stops at the first cell that fails and leaves the cells after it unrun."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20013",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "const menu: Record<string, number> = { green: 3.5, black: 3, mint: 4, oolong: 5 };",
        "",
        "function priceOf(tea: string): number {",
        "  const price = menu[tea];",
        "  if (price === undefined) throw new Error(`no tea called ${tea} on the menu`);",
        "  return price;",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20014",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "priceOf(\"chai\") * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20015",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The failed cell shows the error's name and message, then the line of **this** cell the error came through. **Details** opens the whole stack: each frame gives a function and a line of your TypeScript, not of compiled JavaScript. **Jump** beside the first frame takes you to the `throw` in the cell above.",
        "",
        "Fix it: change `\"chai\"` to `\"mint\"` and run the cell again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t20016",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Try it",
        "",
        "1. With SQL, find the tea that sold the most cups: group by `tea`, sum `cups`, order by it.",
        "2. Write a server cell that returns only the orders of one city with `.filter(...)`, then compare it with the same question asked in the query bar.",
        "3. Change the SVG chart so each bar shows its number of cups at its end.",
        "",
        "Next: `03-typescript`, the types that follow your values from cell to cell."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
